# TraceWeave-Core — keep provenance byte-exact.
#
# candidates/ was produced on a Windows machine (HANDOFF_DISCOVERY.md), so the
# CSVs carry CRLF. corpus/ holds result.env + lock.txt + attempt.log, whose bytes
# back the identity 5-tuple and the classifier-disagreement number in the paper.
# Git's eol normalization would rewrite these on add/checkout; -text disables it
# so what is committed is exactly what the tools emitted.
candidates/** -text
corpus/** -text
corpus.amd64-baseline/** -text

# The paper is binary; never diff or munge it.
*.pdf binary
